Addition
- [N1] Added trace (model 1): init(i1) -> action(n1,"start process") -> action(n2,"gather required items") -> action(n3,"inquire about availability of products") -> action(n4,"wait for invoice") -> action(n5,"review pricing and terms") -> action(n6,"send purchase requisition") -> branch(b1,AND) -> action(n8,"wait for shipment") -> converge(c1) -> action(n9,"receive invoice") -> action(n10,"make payment") -> action(n11,"end process") -> end(e1)

Mutation
- [N2] Node-level mutation: element=action(n5,"review pricing and terms"); source=i5:review the pricing and terms of the items; reason=Drops the explicit qualifier 'of the items', altering the target scope and granularity of the review instruction.
- [N3] Node-level mutation: element=action(n7,"wait for purchase invoice") -> action(n8,"wait for shipment"); source=i7:wait for the purchase invoice and shipment; reason=Splits a single atomic source instruction into two distinct actions bridged by an AND gateway and converge node. This imposes parallel execution and synchronization logic that changes the original granularity and control flow without explicit textual support for concurrency.
